<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Solve simultaneous equations — line and parabola (all x and y values)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Solve the following simultaneous equations: \[ y = {@line@}, \qquad y = {@para@}. \]</p>
<p>Hence find all possible values of \(x\) and \(y\).</p>
<div>Set of \(x\)-values: \( x \in \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<div>Set of \(y\)-values: \( y \in \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(Enter each as a set, e.g. \(\{a,\ b\}\).)</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Both right-hand sides equal \(y\), so set them equal and solve for \(x\):</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
{@para@} &= {@line@}\\
{@quadexpr@} &= 0\\
(x-({@r1@}))(x-({@r2@})) &= 0
\end{align*}
\]
<p>giving \(x={@r1@}\) or \(x={@r2@}\).</p>
<p>Now substitute each \(x\)-value into <em>both</em> equations. Because the equations are simultaneous, both must give the same \(y\):</p>
<p><strong>When \(x={@r1@}\):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Into \(y={@line@}\): \(\quad y={@mm@}\cdot({@r1@})+({@kk@})={@y1@}\).</li>
<li>Into \(y={@para@}\): \(\quad y=({@r1@})^2+({@cc@})={@y1@}\).</li>
</ul>
<p>Both equations give \(y={@y1@}\), so \(({@r1@},\,{@y1@})\) is a solution.</p>
<p><strong>When \(x={@r2@}\):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Into \(y={@line@}\): \(\quad y={@mm@}\cdot({@r2@})+({@kk@})={@y2@}\).</li>
<li>Into \(y={@para@}\): \(\quad y=({@r2@})^2+({@cc@})={@y2@}\).</li>
</ul>
<p>Both equations give \(y={@y2@}\), so \(({@r2@},\,{@y2@})\) is a solution.</p>
<p>Therefore \(x\in{@xset@}\) and \(y\in{@yset@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
